<Step id="STEP_1B_RESUME_OR_START">
      <Goal>Detect a prior aborted attempt at THIS phase before writing or logging anything.</Goal>
      <Action>
        `sdd-task --phase` shows prior PHASES' Handoff, never this phase's OWN Execution Log entries
        — check those separately: sectionExtract ToolCall below and look for this
        phase's heading in the current Round.

        <LogicSwitch on="this phase's own Execution Log entries, current Round">
        - WHEN a `#### <PhaseID>` block already exists WITHOUT a closing `DONE` + Handoff -> a prior
          attempt at this exact phase was interrupted (crash, context limit, killed process — not a
          formal `fix` re-run, which always closes with `DONE`). Read its logged lines in order;
          every already-logged `intro` / `decision` / `verified` line is done semantic work —
          do not redo it or re-log it, and do not re-open files it already reports created unless
          STEP_2 recon finds them missing. A prior receipt is replaced by STEP_5 so it attests the
          resumed attempt's final bytes. Do NOT call `sdd-log
          <ticket> phase <PhaseID>` again — the header already exists; resume by appending the next
          event line into that same block, continuing from where the log stopped.
        - WHEN no such open block exists (fresh phase, or the only block present is a prior Round's
          closed `— re-run: <reason>` attempt that already ends in `DONE` + Handoff) -> fresh start:
          without a fix reason run phaseLog ToolCall below. On a formal fix
          re-run, write exact `— re-run: <reason>` to `.claude/tmp/<task-id>-<phase-id>-log.txt`, then
          run phaseLog ToolCall below
          (`AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE` — the tool is the sole writer, never a manual `Edit`).
        </LogicSwitch>
        <ToolCall owner="phase-worker" result="sectionExtract">npx gennady sdd-extract <ticket> EXECUTION_LOG</ToolCall> Use sectionExtract.
        <ToolCall owner="phase-worker" result="phaseLog">npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> phase <PhaseID></ToolCall> Use phaseLog.
        <ToolCall owner="phase-worker" result="phaseLog">npx gennady sdd-log <ticket> phase <PhaseID> --content-file .claude/tmp/<task-id>-<phase-id>-log.txt</ToolCall> Use phaseLog.
      </Action>
    </Step>